# Third-party notices: the go-emotions model files

The model files beside this document are not the work of the author of
LLM::Classifiers::Emotions, and that distribution's own licence
(Artistic-2.0) does not apply to them. They are Cohee's ONNX export of a
go-emotions classifier, taken unmodified from Hugging Face at revision
`@REVISION@`:

| File | Path in the Hugging Face repository at that revision |
|---|---|
| `tokenizer.json` | `tokenizer.json` |
| `config.json` | `config.json` |
| `model.onnx` | `onnx/model_quantized.onnx`, renamed; contents unchanged |
| `MODEL-CARD.md` | `README.md` (the model card), renamed; contents unchanged |

LLM::Classifiers::Emotions installs these files from the archive
`cohee-goemotions-@BINARY_TAG@.tar.gz`, attached to its GitHub release
`@BINARY_TAG@`. That archive redistributes them, together with this
document, `MODEL-CARD.md` and `LICENSES/`. When the release cannot be
reached, the installer fetches the same files directly from Hugging Face
instead, and checks every one against the same SHA-256.

The full licence texts are in `LICENSES/`: `MIT.txt` and `Apache-2.0.txt`.

## Components

| Component | Licence (SPDX) | Source | Credit |
|---|---|---|---|
| ONNX export, int8-quantised | `MIT` | <https://huggingface.co/Cohee/distilbert-base-uncased-go-emotions-onnx/tree/@REVISION@> | Cohee |
| Distilled go-emotions student model | `MIT` | <https://huggingface.co/joeddav/distilbert-base-uncased-go-emotions-student> | Joe Davison (joeddav) |
| DistilBERT base model, with the BERT vocabulary | `Apache-2.0` | <https://huggingface.co/distilbert/distilbert-base-uncased> | Sanh, Debut, Chaumond and Wolf (DistilBERT, 2019); Devlin, Chang, Lee and Toutanova (BERT, 2018) |
| GoEmotions dataset | `Apache-2.0` | <https://huggingface.co/datasets/google-research-datasets/go_emotions> | Demszky, Movshovitz-Attias, Ko, Cowen, Nemade and Ravi (GoEmotions, 2020) |

## Details

### ONNX export, by Cohee

* Licence: MIT, declared in the metadata of the repository's model card
  (`license: mit`). The repository has no LICENSE file and states no
  copyright notice. `LICENSES/MIT.txt` is the standard MIT text, and its
  `Copyright (c) <year> <copyright holders>` line is the licence's own
  placeholder: upstream never filled it in, so the work is attributed
  here by name and URL instead.
* Source: <https://huggingface.co/Cohee/distilbert-base-uncased-go-emotions-onnx>
  at revision `@REVISION@`.
* In these files: all four of them. The model card describes the export
  as joeddav's student model (below) "converted to ONNX and quantized
  using optimum", and `config.json` names that model as its origin.
* Credit: Cohee.

### Distilled student model, by Joe Davison

* Licence: MIT, declared in the metadata of the repository's model card
  (`license: mit`). The repository has no LICENSE file and states no
  copyright notice, so, as above, the work is attributed here by name
  and URL.
* Source: <https://huggingface.co/joeddav/distilbert-base-uncased-go-emotions-student>.
  The ONNX export does not record which revision of it was converted.
* In these files: the trained weights, which `model.onnx` carries in
  int8-quantised form, and the label set in `config.json`.
* Its model card says it was distilled from the Hugging Face
  transformers zero-shot classification pipeline, run over the
  unlabelled GoEmotions text. That pipeline's NLI teacher model, which
  the card does not name, supplied pseudo-labels only; no part of it is
  in these files.
* Credit: Joe Davison (joeddav).

### DistilBERT base model and the BERT vocabulary

* Licence: Apache-2.0, declared in the repository's metadata. The
  repository ships the Apache License 2.0 as its LICENSE file, the same
  text as `LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt`, with no copyright notice and no
  NOTICE file.
* Source: <https://huggingface.co/distilbert/distilbert-base-uncased>.
* In these files: the architecture and pre-trained base that the student
  model was trained from, and the uncased WordPiece vocabulary embedded
  in `tokenizer.json`. That vocabulary is byte-identical to the
  `vocab.txt` of BERT base uncased
  (<https://huggingface.co/google-bert/bert-base-uncased>, also
  Apache-2.0), the model DistilBERT was distilled from.
* Credit: Victor Sanh, Lysandre Debut, Julien Chaumond and Thomas Wolf,
  "DistilBERT, a distilled version of BERT: smaller, faster, cheaper and
  lighter" (2019, <https://arxiv.org/abs/1910.01108>); and, for BERT,
  Jacob Devlin, Ming-Wei Chang, Kenton Lee and Kristina Toutanova, "BERT:
  Pre-training of Deep Bidirectional Transformers for Language
  Understanding" (2018, <https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.04805>).

### GoEmotions dataset

* Licence: Apache-2.0. The dataset card gives the licence of the GitHub
  repository that houses the dataset,
  <https://github.com/google-research/google-research/blob/master/LICENSE>.
* Source: <https://huggingface.co/datasets/google-research-datasets/go_emotions>;
  the original release is
  <https://github.com/google-research/google-research/tree/master/goemotions>.
* In these files: no text from the dataset. The student model was
  trained on the dataset's comments, without their labels (see above),
  and its 28 labels, GoEmotions' 27 emotion categories plus "neutral",
  are the label names in `config.json`.
* Credit: Dorottya Demszky, Dana Movshovitz-Attias, Jeongwoo Ko, Alan
  Cowen, Gaurav Nemade and Sujith Ravi, "GoEmotions: A Dataset of
  Fine-Grained Emotions", ACL 2020
  (<https://aclanthology.org/2020.acl-main.372/>).

## When these licences were checked

The licences above were checked against Hugging Face on 2026-10-24.
Cohee's repository was checked at the revision these files come from,
`d22488bc83be87678f12eee8a3f65a65de94ef85`. The others were checked at
their revisions current on that day, which are not necessarily the ones
Cohee's export was built from: joeddav's student model at
`82114042047aaa39717090cfb20f3403b73b0215`, DistilBERT at
`12040accade4e8a0f71eabdb258fecc2e7e948be`, BERT base uncased at
`86b5e0934494bd15c9632b12f734a8a67f723594` and GoEmotions at
`add492243ff905527e67aeb8b80c082af02207c3`.

